# Contributing workflow

Never commit to `development` or `main`. GitHub rulesets require pull requests.

1. Open a GitHub issue first (what / who / done-when).
2. Branch `{issue-number}-{short-slug}` from `development`.
3. PR into `development` with `Fixes #N` in the body. Squash merge.
4. Do not delete `development`. Feature branches may be deleted after merge.
5. Production is a later PR from `development` into `main` (release issue).

Push to the `github` remote (`vrigzalejo/iep-progress-tracker`). Do not commit `.env.local` or secrets.

Example: issue #2 → branch `2-add-school-sso` → PR into `development`.
